.Dd July 24, 2026
.Dt ENVFD_CREATE 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm envfd_create
.Nd create a named, descriptor-backed environment value
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/envfd.h
.Ft int
.Fn envfd_create "const char *name" "const struct envfd_create_options *options"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn envfd_create
function creates an environment descriptor containing one named binary value.
The descriptor is initially unwritten.
Each successful
.Xr write 2
atomically replaces the complete value, and each
.Xr read 2
returns a complete snapshot of the current value.
The name is immutable and is descriptive metadata rather than a global lookup
key.
It must be non-empty, fit in
.Dv ENVFD_NAME_MAX
bytes including its terminating null byte, and contain only ASCII letters,
digits,
.Ql . ,
.Ql _ ,
and
.Ql - .
.Pp
The
.Fa options
structure must be zero-initialized except for the documented members:
.Bl -tag -width "Va eco_max_value_size"
.It Va eco_size
Must be
.Li sizeof(struct envfd_create_options) .
.It Va eco_flags
Zero or more of:
.Bl -tag -width "Dv ENVFD_CAPMODE_ONLY"
.It Dv ENVFD_WRITE_ONCE
The first successful write seals the shared object.
Every later write fails with
.Er EROFS ,
including writes through descriptors obtained with
.Xr dup 2 ,
.Xr fork 2 ,
or
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS .
.It Dv ENVFD_CAPMODE_ONLY
Reading, writing, querying information, calling
.Xr fstat 2 ,
and registering an
.Dv EVFILT_ENVFD
event require the calling process to be in Capsicum capability mode.
.El
.It Va eco_access
Must be
.Dv O_RDWR .
After publishing a value, use
.Xr cap_rights_limit 2
to create read-only or write-only capabilities without creating an unusable
initially-unwritten object.
.It Va eco_fdflags
Zero or more of
.Dv FD_CLOEXEC
and
.Dv FD_CLOFORK .
.It Va eco_xfer_state
An initial transfer state:
.Dv CAP_XFER_UNLIMITED ,
.Dv CAP_XFER_ONCE ,
or
.Dv CAP_XFER_NONE .
.It Va eco_cloexec_state
An initial
.Dv CAP_CLOEXEC_*
state.
.It Va eco_clofork_state
An initial
.Dv CAP_CLOFORK_*
state.
.It Va eco_max_value_size
The maximum value size accepted by
.Xr write 2 .
It must not exceed
.Va kern.envfd.max_value_size .
.El
.Pp
The descriptor flags and propagation states are installed atomically with the
new descriptor.
They cannot be observed in their default states by another thread.
.Ss Input and output
A successful write is all-or-nothing.
Short writes are never returned.
A zero-length write publishes an empty value, advances the generation, and,
when
.Dv ENVFD_WRITE_ONCE
is set, seals the object.
.Pp
Reading an unwritten descriptor fails with
.Er ENOATTR .
If the supplied buffer is smaller than the current value,
.Xr read 2
fails with
.Er EMSGSIZE
without returning a partial value.
A zero-length read is handled as a no-op by the generic
.Xr read 2
path and returns zero without examining whether the descriptor is unwritten,
empty, or non-empty.
Call
.Dv ENVFD_GETINFO
and retry the read if a concurrent replacement changes the required size.
Reads do not consume or modify the value.
.Xr pread 2 ,
.Xr pwrite 2 ,
.Xr aio_read 2 ,
.Xr aio_write 2 ,
.Xr lseek 2 ,
.Xr mmap 2 ,
.Xr ftruncate 2 ,
and
.Xr sendfile 2
are not supported.
.Pp
Because EnvFD input and output operations never block,
.Xr poll 2
and
.Xr select 2
report requested ordinary read or write readiness without indicating whether
a value is present or whether a write would succeed.
Use
.Dv EVFILT_ENVFD
to wait for value changes.
.Ss Information
The
.Dv ENVFD_GETINFO
ioctl fills a
.Vt struct envfd_info
with the immutable name, object flags, current state, value size, maximum
size, and generation.
The state is one of:
.Bl -tag -width "Dv ENVFD_STATE_UNWRITTEN"
.It Dv ENVFD_STATE_UNWRITTEN
No successful write has occurred.
.It Dv ENVFD_STATE_READY
A value is present and later writes remain permitted.
.It Dv ENVFD_STATE_SEALED
A value is present and the shared object is permanently write-sealed.
.El
.Pp
Every successful write advances the 64-bit generation, including a write
whose bytes equal the previous value.
.Xr fstat 2
reports the current value size in
.Va st_size .
.Ss Kqueue notification
Environment descriptors support
.Dv EVFILT_ENVFD
with
.Dv EV_CLEAR
semantics.
The requested
.Va fflags
must contain one or both of:
.Bl -tag -width "Dv NOTE_ENVFD_SEALED"
.It Dv NOTE_ENVFD_WRITE
A successful write replaced the value.
.It Dv NOTE_ENVFD_SEALED
The successful write permanently sealed a
.Dv ENVFD_WRITE_ONCE
object.
.El
.Pp
Returned events contain the latest generation in
.Va data
and the latest value size in
.Va ext[0] .
Multiple writes may coalesce into one event; a generation jump identifies
that condition.
Reads and failed writes do not generate events.
The
.Dv EVFILT_READ
and
.Dv EVFILT_WRITE
filters are not supported.
.Pp
To avoid missing a write concurrent with registration, register
.Dv EVFILT_ENVFD
first and then obtain the current generation with
.Dv ENVFD_GETINFO .
.Ss Capsicum
Environment descriptors use existing Capsicum rights:
.Bl -column "CAP_IOCTL" "ENVFD_GETINFO" -offset indent
.It Dv CAP_READ Ta Xr read 2
.It Dv CAP_WRITE Ta Xr write 2
.It Dv CAP_EVENT Ta Dv EVFILT_ENVFD
.It Dv CAP_FSTAT Ta Xr fstat 2
.It Dv CAP_IOCTL Ta Dv ENVFD_GETINFO
.El
.Pp
The
.Dv ENVFD_GETINFO
command must also be present in the descriptor's
.Xr cap_ioctls_limit 2
allowlist when such a list is installed.
.Ss Resource accounting
The kernel charges each object and each immutable value blob to the creating
process's real UID and to system-wide EnvFD totals.
The new and old blobs are both charged while a replacement is being
published.
An old value remains charged while a concurrent reader still holds its
snapshot.
The limits and current totals are exposed under
.Va kern.envfd :
.Bl -tag -width "Va max_user_objects"
.It Va max_objects
Maximum system-wide object count.
.It Va max_bytes
Maximum system-wide kernel bytes.
.It Va max_user_objects
Maximum object count for one real UID.
.It Va max_user_bytes
Maximum kernel bytes for one real UID.
.It Va max_value_size
Maximum configured size of one value.
.It Va objects
Current system-wide object count.
.It Va bytes
Current system-wide kernel bytes.
.El
Setting one of the four object or byte limits to zero disables that
particular limit.
.Ss DTrace
The
.Li envfd
provider exposes
.Li create ,
.Li read ,
.Li write ,
.Li seal ,
.Li notify ,
.Li close ,
and
.Li deny-capmode
probes.
The installed
.Pa /usr/share/dtrace/envfd-events
script provides a lifecycle view without tracing names or value contents.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
On success,
.Fn envfd_create
returns a new file descriptor.
On failure, -1 is returned and
.Va errno
is set.
.Sh ERRORS
In addition to errors from descriptor allocation,
.Fn envfd_create ,
.Xr read 2 ,
and
.Xr write 2
may fail with:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EFBIG
The configured maximum exceeds the system maximum, or a write exceeds the
configured maximum value size.
.It Bq Er ECAPMODE
An operation on an
.Dv ENVFD_CAPMODE_ONLY
descriptor was attempted outside capability mode.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
A structure field, flag, state, access mode, or name is invalid.
.It Bq Er EMFILE
The real UID has reached its EnvFD object limit.
.It Bq Er EMSGSIZE
A read buffer is smaller than the current value.
.It Bq Er ENFILE
The system-wide EnvFD object limit has been reached.
.It Bq Er ENAMETOOLONG
The name is longer than
.Dv ENVFD_NAME_MAX
including its terminating null byte.
.It Bq Er ENOATTR
The descriptor has not been written.
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
An EnvFD memory limit or allocation prevented the operation.
.It Bq Er EOVERFLOW
The generation cannot be advanced.
.It Bq Er EROFS
The shared object is write-sealed.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_enter 2 ,
.Xr cap_ioctls_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_rights_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_xfer_limit 2 ,
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
.Xr kevent 2 ,
.Xr read 2 ,
.Xr write 2 ,
.Xr capsicum 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn envfd_create
function first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
